cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use flybench, cite it as below; cite the connectomes (FlyWire, MaleCNS) and the behavioural papers each task names as well."
title: "flybench: a behavioural benchmark for whole-connectome simulations of Drosophila"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Cho
    given-names: Brandon
repository-code: "https://github.com/brandoncho369/flybench"
url: "https://www.fly-bench.com"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22886374
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22886374
    description: "the concept DOI, every version"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22886375
    description: "this version, 0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-21"
abstract: >
  flybench scores a connectome-constrained neural model (the reference is a uniform leaky
  integrate-and-fire on the FlyWire v783 and MaleCNS v1.0 connectomes) against published fly
  behaviour: 36 tasks, each a stimulus, a readout and thresholds with a citation or a stated
  convention, every one pre-registered as an RFC with predictions before its first run, scored
  with graded margins, ceiling and floor gates, seeds, and shuffled-wiring controls.
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - connectome
  - FlyWire
  - MaleCNS
  - benchmark
  - leaky integrate-and-fire
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A Drosophila computational brain model reveals sensorimotor processing"
    authors:
      - family-names: Shiu
        given-names: Philip K.
    journal: Nature
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07763-9
  - type: article
    title: "Neuronal wiring diagram of an adult brain"
    authors:
      - family-names: Dorkenwald
        given-names: Sven
    journal: Nature
    year: 2024
    doi: 10.1038/s41586-024-07558-y
